---
// Callout aside. Two register-native variants:
//   variant="note"    (default) neutral paper-alt aside, 1px hairline, for general asides.
//   variant="caution"          2px maroon top rule (a hairline, never a side-stripe), for
//                              legal / do-this-or-else emphasis.
// `label` renders a leading DM Mono marker (e.g. "Important", "Deadline") as real,
// accessible text, not CSS-generated content. Omit it for an unmarked aside.
// `maroon` is the original boolean API, kept as an alias for variant="caution" so existing
// <Note maroon> pages keep working. Prefer `variant` on new pages.
//
// MDX: multi-line slot content is now safe. This renders a <div>, so MDX's auto-wrapping <p> is
// valid inside it, exactly as Footnote.astro does. It rendered a <p> until 30 Jul 2026, which made
// a <p> inside a <p> whenever the slot ran to more than one line: invalid, so the browser hoisted
// the text out and you got an empty callout box with its body stranded underneath. The failure was
// silent - the build passed and only the rendered page showed it - and the contract that prevented
// it lived only in this comment, where no call site could see it. That is kb/mistakes-log.md #12,
// whose guard was this warning; it has now been fixed rather than documented. Both forms must
// render identically, so global.css strips the inner paragraph's margins and the wrapper owns the
// spacing (see `.note > p`).
type Variant = 'note' | 'caution';
interface Props { variant?: Variant; maroon?: boolean; label?: string; }
const { variant, maroon = false, label } = Astro.props;
const v: Variant = variant ?? (maroon ? 'caution' : 'note');
const cls = v === 'caution' ? 'note maroon' : 'note';
---
<div class={cls}>{label && <span class="note-k">{label}</span>}<slot /></div>
